# Small / medium files

Prefer **small and medium** Julia files, in the spirit of STATghost (concern-based units, easy to teach and review).

Soft targets (guideline, not hard law):

| Tier | Lines | Use |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Small | ≤ ~80 | one concern (types, auto dispatch, one plot helper) |
| Medium | ~80–160 | coherent feature (binning, summaries, categorical) |
| Avoid | ≫ 200 | split by concern before growing further |

Rules of thumb:

1. One primary concern per file; name the file after that concern.
2. Grow by **adding files**, not by stuffing `Fdth.jl` or a catch-all module file.
3. `src/Fdth.jl` stays a thin `include` hub + exports.
4. Tests may group related cases, but prefer focused `@testset` blocks; split `test/` when a file exceeds ~medium.
5. Do not micro-split (dozens of 10-line files) — readability over fragmentation.
